IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`
IMPORT `ssc1-prelim`
IMPORT `ssc1-class1`
IMPORT `ssc1-class4`

-- Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (United Kingdom), 1992 c. 4.
-- Part I, Class 2 (ss 11 to 12), Class 3 (ss 13 to 14) and Class 3A (ss 14A to 14C) contributions: src lines 474-599.
-- Part agent ssc1, LAYER 1. Source: a plain-text rendering by a converter script, not the official text.
--
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE is the text answering in its own words; NOTHING is "not covered".
-- The figures the Act states in its own words (the Class 2 small profits threshold GBP 7,105, the Class 2 contribution GBP 3.65 and the
-- Class 3 contribution GBP 18.40) are constants "as the Act states it". The Act leaves their alteration to orders and regulations, so the
-- functions that need them take them as inputs and the seat layer passes the constants.
-- Earnings factors and qualifying earnings factors (Schedule 3, ssc8; s 22, ssc2) are inputs.

§ `Part I -- Class 2, Class 3 and Class 3A contributions, ss 11 to 14C`

§§ `s 11 Class 2 contributions`

-- src:476 | (1) This section applies if an earner is in employment as a self-employed earner in a tax year (the “relevant tax year”).
@ref s 11(1) (src:476-476)
GIVEN `the earner is in employment as a self-employed earner in the tax year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 11(1) section 11 applies` MEANS
    IF `the earner is in employment as a self-employed earner in the tax year`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies if an earner is in employment as a self-employed earner in a tax year" (marginal reading M1(a))

-- s 11(3): "relevant profits" means profits, from the employment, in respect of which Class 4 contributions are payable under section 15 for the
-- relevant tax year (or would be payable if the amount of the profits were to exceed the amount in s 15(3)(a)). The amount does not matter, only
-- the kind of profits: s 15(1) is asked of the profits (a profits figure is irrelevant to it).
-- src:478 | (3) “Relevant profits” means profits, from the employment, in respect of which Class 4 contributions are payable under section 15 for the relevant tax year (or would be payable if the amount of the profits were to exceed the amount specified in subsection (3)(a) of that section in excess of which the main Class 4 percentage is payable).
@ref s 11(3) (src:478-478)
GIVEN `the profits are from the employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 15(1) Class 4 contributions are payable on the profits, or would be if their amount exceeded the lower profits limit` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 11(3) the profits are relevant profits` MEANS
    IF `the profits are from the employment` AND `s 15(1) Class 4 contributions are payable on the profits, or would be if their amount exceeded the lower profits limit` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE
        IF NOT `the profits are from the employment`
        THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Relevant profits” means profits, from the employment, in respect of which Class 4 contributions are payable under section 15"
        ELSE
            IF `s 15(1) Class 4 contributions are payable on the profits, or would be if their amount exceeded the lower profits limit` EQUALS JUST FALSE
            THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the same definition
            ELSE NOTHING       -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether section 15 reaches the profits was not answered (s 15(1) returns NOTHING for profits outside its three limbs)

-- src:479 | (4) For the purposes of this Act—
-- src:480 | (a) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:481 | (b) the “small profits threshold” is £7,105.
@ref s 11(4)(b) (src:479-481)
`s 11(4)(b) the small profits threshold as the Act states it` MEANS 7105

-- s 11(7): no Class 2 contribution is to be paid or treated as paid for a week before the week in which the earner attains 16 or after
-- the week in which the earner attains pensionable age. "the week in which the earner attains" an age is a plain fact the earner can state
-- (s 173 answers ages at a date, not weeks; the week is the Sunday-start week of s 122(1), ssc5).
-- src:489 | (7) No Class 2 contributions are to be paid or treated as paid under this section in respect of any week in the relevant tax year—
-- src:490 | (a) before that in which the earner attains the age of 16, or
-- src:491 | (b) after that in which the earner attains pensionable age.
@ref s 11(7) (src:489-491)
GIVEN `the week is before the week in which the earner attains the age of 16` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the week is after the week in which the earner attains pensionable age` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 11(7) a Class 2 contribution is to be paid or treated as paid in respect of the week` MEANS
    IF `the week is before the week in which the earner attains the age of 16` OR `the week is after the week in which the earner attains pensionable age`
    THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No Class 2 contributions are to be paid or treated as paid under this section in respect of any week ... (a) before that in which the earner attains the age of 16, or (b) after that in which the earner attains pensionable age"
    ELSE NOTHING       -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is for weeks before or after those; otherwise the subsection is silent

-- s 11(5A), (5B), (5C): an earner with relevant profits of, or exceeding, the small profits threshold is treated, for relevant purposes
-- (provisions about benefits and other entitlements that apply by reference to Class 2 contributions), as having actually paid a Class 2
-- contribution for each week in the relevant tax year that the earner is in the employment.
-- src:483 | (5A) Subsection (5B) applies to an earner who has, for the relevant tax year, relevant profits of, or exceeding, the small profits threshold....
-- src:484 | (5B) An earner to whom this subsection applies is treated, for relevant purposes, as having actually paid a Class 2 contribution ... in respect of each week in the relevant tax year that the earner is in the employment.
-- src:485 | (5C) “For relevant purposes” means for the purposes of provision made by or under an enactment that—
-- src:486 | (a) is provision relating to benefits, or any other entitlement, provided for by or under an enactment, and
-- src:487 | (b) applies by reference (however framed) to Class 2 contributions (whether or not the provision refers to contributions treated as paid).
@ref s 11(5A), s 11(5B), s 11(5C) (src:483-487)
GIVEN `s 11(1) section 11 applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the earner is in the employment in the week` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the earner's relevant profits for the relevant tax year` IS A NUMBER
      `s 11(4)(b) the small profits threshold` IS A NUMBER
      `s 11(7) a Class 2 contribution is to be paid or treated as paid in respect of the week` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 11(5B) the earner is treated for relevant purposes as having actually paid a Class 2 contribution in respect of the week` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 11(7) a Class 2 contribution is to be paid or treated as paid in respect of the week` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): subsection (7), "No Class 2 contributions are to be paid or treated as paid under this section" for that week
        IF `s 11(1) section 11 applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): subsection (1), "This section applies if an earner is in employment as a self-employed earner in a tax year" (marginal reading M1(a))
        IF NOT (`s 11(1) section 11 applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the answer of section 11(1) was not supplied
        IF NOT `the earner is in the employment in the week` THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in respect of each week in the relevant tax year that the earner is in the employment"
        IF `the earner's relevant profits for the relevant tax year` AT LEAST `s 11(4)(b) the small profits threshold` THEN JUST TRUE    -- (5A): "of, or exceeding, the small profits threshold"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (5B) applies to "an earner to whom this subsection applies"; (5A) names the earner with relevant profits of, or exceeding, the threshold and says no more

-- s 11(6): an earner who does not have relevant profits of, or exceeding, the small profits threshold may pay a Class 2 contribution of GBP 3.65 for any
-- week in the relevant tax year that the earner is in the employment. The Treasury may bar it by regulations (s 11(9)(b)).
-- src:488 | (6) If the earner does not have relevant profits of, or exceeding, the small profits threshold, the earner may pay a Class 2 contribution of £3.65 in respect of any week in the relevant tax year that the earner is in the employment.
@ref s 11(6) (src:488-488)
`s 11(6) the Class 2 contribution as the Act states it` MEANS 3.65

-- src:488 | (6) If the earner does not have relevant profits of, or exceeding, the small profits threshold, the earner may pay a Class 2 contribution of £3.65 in respect of any week in the relevant tax year that the earner is in the employment.
@ref s 11(6) (src:488-488)
GIVEN `s 11(1) section 11 applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the earner is in the employment in the week` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the earner's relevant profits for the relevant tax year` IS A NUMBER
      `s 11(4)(b) the small profits threshold` IS A NUMBER
      `s 11(7) a Class 2 contribution is to be paid or treated as paid in respect of the week` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `regulations under subsection (9)(b) provide that Class 2 contributions under subsection (6) may not be paid in the case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 11(6) the earner may pay a Class 2 contribution in respect of the week` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 11(7) a Class 2 contribution is to be paid or treated as paid in respect of the week` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): subsection (7), "No Class 2 contributions are to be paid ... in respect of any week" before the week of attaining 16 or after the week of attaining pensionable age
        IF `s 11(1) section 11 applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): subsection (1), "This section applies if an earner is in employment as a self-employed earner in a tax year" (marginal reading M1(a))
        IF NOT (`s 11(1) section 11 applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the answer of section 11(1) was not supplied
        IF NOT `the earner is in the employment in the week` THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in respect of any week in the relevant tax year that the earner is in the employment"
        IF `the earner's relevant profits for the relevant tax year` AT LEAST `s 11(4)(b) the small profits threshold` THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the earner does not have relevant profits of, or exceeding, the small profits threshold, the earner may pay" (marginal reading M1(a): a failed "if" counts as the text's no)
        IF `regulations under subsection (9)(b) provide that Class 2 contributions under subsection (6) may not be paid in the case` THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): subsection (9)(b), regulations may bar payment
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- PLAN.md seam S4 (ssc2 s 22 asks): the number of weeks for which a Class 2 contribution was paid in the tax year. A week counts when the
-- earner is treated as having paid under (5B) or paid under (6).
DECLARE `s 11 Week of the tax year` HAS
    `s 11 a Class 2 contribution is treated as actually paid under subsection (5B)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 11 a Class 2 contribution was paid under subsection (6)`                    IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:484 | (5B) An earner to whom this subsection applies is treated, for relevant purposes, as having actually paid a Class 2 contribution ... in respect of each week in the relevant tax year that the earner is in the employment.
@ref s 11(5B) (src:484-484)
GIVEN weeks IS A LIST OF `s 11 Week of the tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 11 the number of weeks for which a Class 2 contribution was paid in the tax year` MEANS
    count (filter (GIVEN w YIELD w's `s 11 a Class 2 contribution is treated as actually paid under subsection (5B)` OR w's `s 11 a Class 2 contribution was paid under subsection (6)`) weeks)

§§ `s 11A Relevant profits to be included in self assessment tax return`

DECLARE `s 11A(1) Purpose for which Part 2 of the Taxes Management Act 1970 is applied` IS ONE OF
    `s 11A(1) establishing whether an earner has relevant profits of, or exceeding, the small profits threshold for a tax year`
    `s 11A(1) another purpose`

-- src:505 | (1) Part 2 (returns) of the Taxes Management Act 1970 applies, with the necessary modifications, for the purpose of establishing whether an earner has relevant profits of, or exceeding, the small profits threshold for a tax year, as it applies for the purpose of establishing the amounts in which a person is chargeable to income tax and capital gains tax for a year of assessment.
@ref s 11A(1) (src:505-505)
GIVEN purpose IS A `s 11A(1) Purpose for which Part 2 of the Taxes Management Act 1970 is applied`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 11A(1) Part 2 of the Taxes Management Act 1970 applies, with the necessary modifications, for the purpose` MEANS
    CONSIDER purpose
    WHEN `s 11A(1) establishing whether an earner has relevant profits of, or exceeding, the small profits threshold for a tax year` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 11A(1) another purpose` THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): section 11A(1) speaks of that purpose only

-- src:506 | (2) In this section “relevant profits” has the meaning it has in section 11 (Class 2 contributions).
@ref s 11A(2) (src:506-506)
GIVEN `the profits are relevant profits within the meaning of section 11` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 11A(2) the profits are relevant profits` MEANS `the profits are relevant profits within the meaning of section 11`

§§ `s 12 Late paid Class 2 contributions`

-- src:508 | (1) This section applies to any Class 2 contribution under section 11(6) paid in respect of a week falling within a tax year (“the contribution year") earlier than the tax year in which it is paid (“the payment year").
@ref s 12(1) (src:508-508)
GIVEN `it is a Class 2 contribution under section 11(6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contribution year` IS A `Tax year`
      `the payment year` IS A `Tax year`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12(1) section 12 applies to the contribution` MEANS
    IF     `it is a Class 2 contribution under section 11(6)`
       AND `the contribution year`'s `calendar year in which it begins` LESS THAN `the payment year`'s `calendar year in which it begins`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies to any Class 2 contribution under section 11(6) paid in respect of a week falling within a tax year earlier than the tax year in which it is paid"

-- src:520 | (8) In this section—
-- src:521 | “ordinary contribution” means a contribution of the amount specified in section 11(6); and
-- src:522 | “higher-rate contribution” means a contribution of an amount provided for in regulations under section 11(8).
@ref s 12(8) (src:520-522)
GIVEN `the contribution is of the amount specified in section 11(6)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12(8) the contribution is an ordinary contribution` MEANS
    IF `the contribution is of the amount specified in section 11(6)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“ordinary contribution” means a contribution of the amount specified in section 11(6)"

-- s 12(3)(a) and (b): the earner pays after the end of the tax year immediately following the contribution year (so in the second year after it or
-- later), and the weekly rate for the week in the contribution year differs from the weekly rate applicable at the time of payment.
-- src:510 | (3) Subject to subsections (4) and (6) below, in any case where—
-- src:511 | (a) the earner pays an ordinary contribution to which this section applies after the end of the tax year immediately following the contribution year; and
-- src:512 | (b) the weekly rate of ordinary contributions for the week in respect of which the contribution was payable in the contribution year differs from the weekly rate applicable at the time of payment in the payment year,
@ref s 12(3) (src:510-512)
GIVEN `the contribution year` IS A `Tax year`
      `the payment year` IS A `Tax year`
      `the weekly rate in the contribution year` IS A NUMBER
      `the weekly rate applicable at the time of payment in the payment year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 12(3)(a) and (b) the contribution is paid after the end of the tax year immediately following the contribution year, and the weekly rates differ` MEANS
        `the payment year`'s `calendar year in which it begins` AT LEAST (`the contribution year`'s `calendar year in which it begins` PLUS 2)
    AND NOT (`the weekly rate in the contribution year` EQUALS `the weekly rate applicable at the time of payment in the payment year`)

-- s 12(2) and (3): the amount the earner would have had to pay in the contribution year; but where an ordinary contribution is paid after the
-- end of the tax year immediately following the contribution year and the weekly rate then differs from the rate at payment, the highest weekly
-- rate of ordinary contributions in the period from the week in respect of which it is paid to the day it is paid. Subject to regulations under (4) and (6).
-- src:509 | (2) Subject to subsections (3) and (4) below, the amount of a contribution to which this section applies shall be the amount which the earner would have had to pay if he had paid the contribution in the contribution year.
-- src:510 | (3) Subject to subsections (4) and (6) below, in any case where—
-- src:511 | (a) the earner pays an ordinary contribution to which this section applies after the end of the tax year immediately following the contribution year; and
-- src:512 | (b) the weekly rate of ordinary contributions for the week in respect of which the contribution was payable in the contribution year differs from the weekly rate applicable at the time of payment in the payment year,
-- src:513 | the amount of the contribution shall be computed by reference to the highest weekly rate of ordinary contributions in the period beginning with the week in respect of which the contribution is paid and ending with the day on which it is paid.
@ref s 12(2) (src:509-513)
GIVEN `s 12(1) section 12 applies to the contribution` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 12(8) the contribution is an ordinary contribution` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the contribution year` IS A `Tax year`
      `the payment year` IS A `Tax year`
      `the weekly rate in the contribution year` IS A NUMBER
      `the weekly rate applicable at the time of payment in the payment year` IS A NUMBER
      `the weekly rates of ordinary contributions in the period beginning with the week in respect of which the contribution is paid and ending with the day on which it is paid` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      `regulations under subsection (4) or (6) apply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 12(2) the amount of the late paid Class 2 contribution` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`s 12(1) section 12 applies to the contribution` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): section 12 applies to a contribution under s 11(6) paid for a week in an earlier tax year
        IF `regulations under subsection (4) or (6) apply` THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Subject to subsections (3) and (4)", regulations
        IF NOT (`s 12(3)(a) and (b) the contribution is paid after the end of the tax year immediately following the contribution year, and the weekly rates differ` `the contribution year` `the payment year` `the weekly rate in the contribution year` `the weekly rate applicable at the time of payment in the payment year`) THEN JUST `the weekly rate in the contribution year`    -- (2): "the amount which the earner would have had to pay if he had paid the contribution in the contribution year"
        IF `s 12(8) the contribution is an ordinary contribution` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST `the weekly rate in the contribution year`    -- (3) speaks of "an ordinary contribution"; a higher-rate contribution stays with (2)
        IF `s 12(8) the contribution is an ordinary contribution` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN
            CONSIDER `the weekly rates of ordinary contributions in the period beginning with the week in respect of which the contribution is paid and ending with the day on which it is paid`
            WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no rates in the period were supplied
            WHEN first FOLLOWED BY rest THEN JUST (maximum (first FOLLOWED BY rest))    -- (3): "the highest weekly rate of ordinary contributions in the period"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the contribution is an ordinary contribution was not answered

§§ `s 13 Class 3 contributions`

-- src:525 | (1) The Treasury shall by regulations provide for earners and others, if over the age of 16, to be entitled if they so wish, but subject to any prescribed conditions, to pay Class 3 contributions; and, subject to the following provisions of this section, the amount of a Class 3 contribution shall be £18.40.
@ref s 13(1) (src:525-525)
`s 13(1) the amount of a Class 3 contribution as the Act states it` MEANS 18.40

-- s 13(1): the regulations provide for earners and others, if over the age of 16, to be entitled, if they so wish and subject to prescribed
-- conditions, to pay Class 3 contributions. "over the age of 16" is s 173(a) (input K2). The regulations themselves are outside these sources.
-- src:525 | (1) The Treasury shall by regulations provide for earners and others, if over the age of 16, to be entitled if they so wish, but subject to any prescribed conditions, to pay Class 3 contributions; and, subject to the following provisions of this section, the amount of a Class 3 contribution shall be £18.40.
@ref s 13(1) (src:525-525)
GIVEN `s 173(a) the person is over 16` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the regulations, subject to the prescribed conditions, entitle the person to pay` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 13(1) the person is entitled to pay a Class 3 contribution` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 173(a) the person is over 16`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the answer of section 173(a) was not supplied
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Treasury shall by regulations provide for earners and others, if over the age of 16, to be entitled" (marginal reading M1(a))
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the regulations, subject to the prescribed conditions, entitle the person to pay`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the entitlement is created by regulations and "subject to any prescribed conditions"

-- s 13(2): payment of Class 3 contributions is allowed only with a view to enabling the contributor to satisfy conditions of entitlement to
-- benefit by acquiring the requisite earnings factor for the purposes described in s 22 (ssc2: seam S9).
-- src:526 | (2) Payment of Class 3 contributions shall be allowed only with a view to enabling the contributor to satisfy ... conditions of entitlement to benefit by acquiring the requisite earnings factor for the purposes described in section 22 below.
@ref s 13(2) (src:526-526)
GIVEN `s 22 the payment is with a view to acquiring the requisite earnings factor for the purposes described` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 13(2) payment of the Class 3 contribution is allowed` MEANS
    IF `s 22 the payment is with a view to acquiring the requisite earnings factor for the purposes described`
    THEN NOTHING       -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "only with a view to" states a necessary condition; meeting it does not by itself allow the payment
    ELSE JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Payment of Class 3 contributions shall be allowed only with a view to enabling the contributor to satisfy ... conditions of entitlement to benefit by acquiring the requisite earnings factor"

-- s 13(5): the payment year is the tax year in which a contribution is paid; the contribution year is the earlier year mentioned in (4).
-- src:529 | (5) In this section—
-- src:530 | “the payment year” means the tax year in which a contribution is paid; and
-- src:531 | “the contribution year” means the earlier year mentioned in subsection (4) above.
@ref s 13(5) (src:529-531)
GIVEN `the tax year in which the contribution is paid` IS A `Tax year`
GIVETH A `Tax year`
`s 13(5) the payment year` MEANS `the tax year in which the contribution is paid`

-- src:529 | (5) In this section—
-- src:530 | “the payment year” means the tax year in which a contribution is paid; and
-- src:531 | “the contribution year” means the earlier year mentioned in subsection (4) above.
@ref s 13(5) (src:529-531)
GIVEN `the earlier tax year in respect of which the contribution is paid` IS A `Tax year`
GIVETH A `Tax year`
`s 13(5) the contribution year` MEANS `the earlier tax year in respect of which the contribution is paid`

-- s 13(4) and (6): the amount of a contribution for an earlier tax year is that of the earlier year, unless it is paid after the end of the next
-- tax year but one following the contribution year and the amounts differ, when it is the highest of the two amounts and of any other amount in
-- the intervening period; or unless regulations under (7) apply.
-- src:528 | (4) The amount of a Class 3 contribution in respect of a tax year earlier than the tax year in which it is paid shall be the same as if it had been paid in the earlier year and in respect of that year, unless it falls to be calculated in accordance with subsection (6) below or regulations under subsection (7) below.
-- src:529 | (5) In this section—
-- src:530 | “the payment year” means the tax year in which a contribution is paid; and
-- src:531 | “the contribution year” means the earlier year mentioned in subsection (4) above.
-- src:532 | (6) Subject to subsection (7) below, in any case where—
-- src:533 | (a) a Class 3 contribution is paid after the end of the next tax year but one following the contribution year; and
-- src:534 | (b) the amount of a Class 3 contribution applicable had the contribution been paid in the contribution year differs from the amount of a Class 3 contribution applicable at the time of payment in the payment year,
-- src:535 | the amount of the contribution shall be computed by reference to the highest of those two amounts and of any other amount of a Class 3 contribution in the intervening period.
@ref s 13(4), s 13(6) (src:528-535)
GIVEN `the contribution year` IS A `Tax year`
      `the payment year` IS A `Tax year`
      `the amount of a Class 3 contribution applicable had the contribution been paid in the contribution year` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of a Class 3 contribution applicable at the time of payment in the payment year` IS A NUMBER
      `any other amounts of a Class 3 contribution in the intervening period` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      `regulations under subsection (7) apply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 13(4) the amount of the Class 3 contribution for the earlier tax year` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the payment year`'s `calendar year in which it begins` AT MOST `the contribution year`'s `calendar year in which it begins` THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (4) speaks of "a tax year earlier than the tax year in which it is paid"
        IF `regulations under subsection (7) apply` THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "unless it falls to be calculated in accordance with ... regulations under subsection (7)"
        IF     `the payment year`'s `calendar year in which it begins` AT LEAST (`the contribution year`'s `calendar year in which it begins` PLUS 3)
           AND NOT (`the amount of a Class 3 contribution applicable had the contribution been paid in the contribution year` EQUALS `the amount of a Class 3 contribution applicable at the time of payment in the payment year`)
        THEN JUST (maximum (`the amount of a Class 3 contribution applicable had the contribution been paid in the contribution year` FOLLOWED BY (`the amount of a Class 3 contribution applicable at the time of payment in the payment year` FOLLOWED BY `any other amounts of a Class 3 contribution in the intervening period`)))    -- (6): "the highest of those two amounts and of any other amount"
        OTHERWISE JUST `the amount of a Class 3 contribution applicable had the contribution been paid in the contribution year`    -- (4): "the same as if it had been paid in the earlier year"

-- PLAN.md seam S4: the number of weeks for which a Class 3 contribution was paid in the tax year. s 13(3): regulations may appropriate contributions
-- paid in one tax year to the earnings factor of another.
-- src:527 | (3) The Secretary of State may by regulations provide for Class 3 contributions, although paid in one tax year, to be appropriated in prescribed circumstances to the earnings factor of another tax year.
@ref s 13(3) (src:527-527)
GIVEN `the number of weeks of the tax year for which Class 3 contributions were paid in the tax year` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of weeks of other tax years for which contributions are appropriated to the earnings factor of the tax year` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of weeks of the tax year for which contributions are appropriated to the earnings factor of another tax year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 13 the number of weeks for which a Class 3 contribution was paid in the tax year` MEANS
    `the number of weeks of the tax year for which Class 3 contributions were paid in the tax year`
    PLUS `the number of weeks of other tax years for which contributions are appropriated to the earnings factor of the tax year`
    MINUS `the number of weeks of the tax year for which contributions are appropriated to the earnings factor of another tax year`

§§ `s 13A Right to pay additional Class 3 contributions in certain cases`

-- s 13A(2): a missing year is a tax year not earlier than 1975-76 in respect of which the person would be entitled under regulations under s 13 to pay Class 3
-- contributions but for a limit on the time within which they may be paid. 1975-76 begins in 1975.
-- src:539 | (2) A missing year is a tax year not earlier than 1975-76 in respect of which the person would under regulations under section 13 be entitled to pay Class 3 contributions but for a limit on the time within which contributions may be paid in respect of that year.
@ref s 13A(2) (src:539-539)
GIVEN year IS A `Tax year`
      `the person would under regulations under section 13 be entitled to pay Class 3 contributions in respect of the year but for a limit on the time within which contributions may be paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 13A(2) the tax year is a missing year` MEANS
    IF     year's `calendar year in which it begins` AT LEAST 1975
       AND `the person would under regulations under section 13 be entitled to pay Class 3 contributions in respect of the year but for a limit on the time within which contributions may be paid`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A missing year is a tax year not earlier than 1975-76 in respect of which the person would under regulations under section 13 be entitled to pay Class 3 contributions but for a limit on the time" (marginal reading M3: a defining "is" is read like "means")

-- s 13A(3): not entitled to pay contributions under this section in respect of more than 6 tax years.
-- src:540 | (3) A person is not entitled to pay contributions in respect of more than 6 tax years under this section.
@ref s 13A(3) (src:540-540)
GIVEN `the number of tax years, counting this one, in respect of which the person would have paid contributions under this section` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 13A(3) the person is entitled to pay a contribution under section 13A for the tax year` MEANS
    IF `the number of tax years, counting this one, in respect of which the person would have paid contributions under this section` GREATER THAN 6
    THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is not entitled to pay contributions in respect of more than 6 tax years under this section"
    ELSE NOTHING       -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is on "more than 6 tax years"; within six the subsection is silent

-- s 13A(4): not entitled to pay any contribution under the section after the end of 6 years beginning with the day on which the person attains
-- pensionable age. The end of 6 years beginning with a day is the day before its sixth anniversary. For a day of 29 February the anniversary in a
-- year without a 29 February is not given by the text (fork F4): NOTHING.
-- src:541 | (4) A person is not entitled to pay any contribution under this section after the end of 6 years beginning with the day on which he attains pensionable age.
@ref s 13A(4) (src:541-541)
GIVEN `the day on which the person attains pensionable age` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 13A(4) the last day on which a contribution may be paid under section 13A` MEANS
    IF DATE_DAY `the day on which the person attains pensionable age` EQUALS 29 AND DATE_MONTH `the day on which the person attains pensionable age` EQUALS 2
    THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): fork F4, the text does not say what the anniversary of 29 February is in a year without one
    ELSE JUST ((`add years` `the day on which the person attains pensionable age` 6) MINUS 1)

-- src:541 | (4) A person is not entitled to pay any contribution under this section after the end of 6 years beginning with the day on which he attains pensionable age.
@ref s 13A(4) (src:541-541)
GIVEN `the day on which the person attains pensionable age` IS A DATE
      `the day of payment` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 13A(4) the person is entitled to pay a contribution under section 13A on the day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 13A(4) the last day on which a contribution may be paid under section 13A` `the day on which the person attains pensionable age`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): fork F4
    WHEN JUST last THEN
        IF `the day of payment` GREATER THAN last
        THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is not entitled to pay any contribution under this section after the end of 6 years beginning with the day on which he attains pensionable age"
        ELSE NOTHING       -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is on payments after that day; up to it the subsection is silent

-- s 13A(6): the first condition is that the person attained or will attain pensionable age in the period beginning with 6 April 2008 and ending with 5 April 2015.
-- src:543 | (6) The first condition is that the person attained or will attain pensionable age in the period—
-- src:544 | (a) beginning with 6th April 2008, and
-- src:545 | (b) ending with 5th April 2015.
@ref s 13A(6) (src:543-545)
GIVEN `the day on which the person attained or will attain pensionable age` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 13A(6) the first condition is satisfied` MEANS
    IF `the day on which the person attained or will attain pensionable age` AT LEAST (Date 6 4 2008) AND `the day on which the person attained or will attain pensionable age` AT MOST (Date 5 4 2015)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is an eligible person if the following conditions are satisfied. The first condition is that the person attained or will attain pensionable age in the period" (marginal reading M1(a))

-- s 13A(8): a year is one to which subsection (8) applies if (a) the person paid or was credited with contributions of a relevant class for paragraph 5
-- or 5A of Schedule 3, or credited (1987-88 onward) with earnings, and (b) the earnings factor derived as in (9) is not less than the qualifying
-- earnings factor for the year. The earnings factor and the qualifying earnings factor are inputs (Schedule 3, ssc8).
-- src:547 | (8) This subsection applies if—
-- src:548 | (a) the year is one in respect of which the person has paid or been credited with contributions that are of a relevant class for the purposes of paragraph 5 or 5A of Schedule 3 or been credited (in the case of 1987-88 or any subsequent year) with earnings, and
-- src:549 | (b) in the case of that year, the earnings factor derived as mentioned in subsection (9) is not less than the qualifying earnings factor for that year.
@ref s 13A(8) (src:547-549)
GIVEN `the person has paid or been credited with contributions of a relevant class for the purposes of paragraph 5 or 5A of Schedule 3, or been credited with earnings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the earnings factor derived as mentioned in subsection (9)` IS A NUMBER
      `the qualifying earnings factor for the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 13A(8) the year is a year to which subsection (8) applies` MEANS
    IF     `the person has paid or been credited with contributions of a relevant class for the purposes of paragraph 5 or 5A of Schedule 3, or been credited with earnings`
       AND `the earnings factor derived as mentioned in subsection (9)` AT LEAST `the qualifying earnings factor for the year`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This subsection applies if (a) ... and (b) ... not less than the qualifying earnings factor for that year" (marginal reading M1(a))

-- s 13A(9)(a)(i): for 1987-88 and later the earnings factor of s 13A(8)(b) is derived from so much of the person's earnings as did not exceed the
-- upper earnings limit and upon which primary Class 1 contributions were paid or treated as paid (or earnings credited); the conversion of
-- those earnings and of Class 2 or Class 3 contributions into an earnings factor is Schedule 3's (ssc8), so the factor itself stays an input.
-- src:550 | (9) For the purposes of subsection (8)(b) the earnings factor—
-- src:551 | (a) in the case of 1987-88 or any subsequent year, is that which is derived from—
-- src:552 | (i) so much of the person's earnings as did not exceed the upper earnings limit and upon which such of the contributions mentioned in subsection (8)(a) as are primary Class 1 contributions were paid or treated as paid or earnings credited, and
-- src:553 | (ii) any Class 2 or Class 3 contributions for the year, or
-- src:554 | (b) in the case of any earlier year, is that which is derived from the contributions mentioned in subsection (8)(a).
@ref s 13A(9) (src:550-554)
GIVEN `the person's earnings upon which primary Class 1 contributions were paid or treated as paid, or earnings credited` IS A NUMBER
      `the upper earnings limit` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 13A(9)(a)(i) the earnings from which the earnings factor is derived` MEANS min `the person's earnings upon which primary Class 1 contributions were paid or treated as paid, or earnings credited` `the upper earnings limit`

-- s 13A(10): for a person who attained or will attain pensionable age before 6 April 2010, a year in which the person was precluded from regular
-- employment by responsibilities at home within the meaning of regulations under paragraph 5(7) of Schedule 3.
-- src:555 | (10) This subsection applies (in the case of a person who attained or will attain pensionable age before 6th April 2010) if the year is one in which the person was precluded from regular employment by responsibilities at home within the meaning of regulations under paragraph 5(7) of Schedule 3.
@ref s 13A(10) (src:555-555)
GIVEN `the day on which the person attained or will attain pensionable age` IS A DATE
      `the year is one in which the person was precluded from regular employment by responsibilities at home within the meaning of regulations under paragraph 5(7) of Schedule 3` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 13A(10) the year is a year to which subsection (10) applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the day on which the person attained or will attain pensionable age` AT LEAST (Date 6 4 2010) THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(in the case of a person who attained or will attain pensionable age before 6th April 2010)"
        IF `the year is one in which the person was precluded from regular employment by responsibilities at home within the meaning of regulations under paragraph 5(7) of Schedule 3` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This subsection applies ... if the year is one in which the person was precluded from regular employment by responsibilities at home" (marginal reading M1(a))

-- src:546 | (7) The second condition is that there are at least 20 tax years each of which is a year to which subsection (8) or (10) applies.
@ref s 13A(7) (src:546-546)
GIVEN `the number of tax years each of which is a year to which subsection (8) or (10) applies` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 13A(7) the second condition is satisfied` MEANS
    IF `the number of tax years each of which is a year to which subsection (8) or (10) applies` AT LEAST 20
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The second condition is that there are at least 20 tax years each of which is a year to which subsection (8) or (10) applies" (marginal reading M1(a))

-- src:556 | (11) The third condition applies only if the person attained or will attain pensionable age before 6th April 2010.
@ref s 13A(11) (src:556-556)
GIVEN `the day on which the person attained or will attain pensionable age` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 13A(11) the third condition applies` MEANS
    IF `the day on which the person attained or will attain pensionable age` LESS THAN (Date 6 4 2010)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The third condition applies only if the person attained or will attain pensionable age before 6th April 2010"

-- src:557 | (12) That condition is that—
-- src:558 | (a) the person has, in respect of any one tax year before that in which he attains pensionable age, actually paid contributions that are of a relevant class for the purposes of paragraph 5 of Schedule 3, and
-- src:559 | (b) in the case of that year, the earnings factor derived as mentioned in subsection (13) is not less than the qualifying earnings factor for that year.
@ref s 13A(12) (src:557-559)
GIVEN `the person has, in respect of any one tax year before that in which he attains pensionable age, actually paid contributions of a relevant class for the purposes of paragraph 5 of Schedule 3` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the earnings factor derived as mentioned in subsection (13)` IS A NUMBER
      `the qualifying earnings factor for the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 13A(12) the third condition is satisfied` MEANS
    IF     `the person has, in respect of any one tax year before that in which he attains pensionable age, actually paid contributions of a relevant class for the purposes of paragraph 5 of Schedule 3`
       AND `the earnings factor derived as mentioned in subsection (13)` AT LEAST `the qualifying earnings factor for the year`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "That condition is that (a) ... and (b) ... not less than the qualifying earnings factor for that year" (marginal reading M1(a))

-- s 13A(13)(a)(i): the same rule for the earnings factor of s 13A(12)(b), counting Class 1 contributions paid or treated as paid.
-- src:560 | (13) For the purposes of subsection (12)(b) the earnings factor—
-- src:561 | (a) in the case of 1987-88 or any subsequent year, is that which is derived from—
-- src:562 | (i) so much of the person's earnings as did not exceed the upper earnings limit and upon which such of the contributions mentioned in subsection (12)(a) as are primary Class 1 contributions were paid or treated as paid, and
-- src:563 | (ii) any Class 2 or Class 3 contributions for the year, or
-- src:564 | (b) in the case of any earlier year, is that which is derived from the contributions mentioned in subsection (12)(a).
@ref s 13A(13) (src:560-564)
GIVEN `the person's earnings upon which primary Class 1 contributions were paid or treated as paid` IS A NUMBER
      `the upper earnings limit` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 13A(13)(a)(i) the earnings from which the earnings factor is derived` MEANS min `the person's earnings upon which primary Class 1 contributions were paid or treated as paid` `the upper earnings limit`

-- s 13A(5): a person is an eligible person if the conditions are satisfied. The third condition counts only for a person to whom it applies.
-- src:542 | (5) A person is an eligible person if the following conditions are satisfied.
@ref s 13A(5) (src:542-542)
GIVEN first IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      second IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the third condition applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      third IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 13A(5) the person is an eligible person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF first EQUALS JUST FALSE OR second EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is an eligible person if the following conditions are satisfied" (marginal reading M1(a))
        IF `the third condition applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND third EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the same, as to the third condition
        IF first EQUALS JUST TRUE AND second EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the third condition applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF first EQUALS JUST TRUE AND second EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the third condition applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND third EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a condition was not answered

-- s 13A(1) with ss 13A(3) and (4): an eligible person is entitled, if he so wishes but subject to prescribed conditions, to pay Class 3 contributions for a missing year.
-- src:538 | (1) An eligible person is entitled, if he so wishes, but subject to any conditions prescribed by regulations made by the Treasury and to the following provisions of this section, to pay Class 3 contributions in respect of a missing year.
@ref s 13A(1) (src:538-538)
GIVEN eligible IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `missing year` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 13A(3) the person is entitled to pay a contribution under section 13A for the tax year` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 13A(4) the person is entitled to pay a contribution under section 13A on the day` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the prescribed conditions are satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 13A(1) an eligible person is entitled to pay a Class 3 contribution in respect of the missing year, having regard to subsections (3) and (4)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 13A(3) the person is entitled to pay a contribution under section 13A for the tax year` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): subsection (3), "A person is not entitled to pay contributions in respect of more than 6 tax years under this section"
        IF `s 13A(4) the person is entitled to pay a contribution under section 13A on the day` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): subsection (4), "not entitled to pay any contribution under this section after the end of 6 years"
        IF eligible EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `missing year` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the prescribed conditions are satisfied` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An eligible person is entitled ... to pay Class 3 contributions in respect of a missing year", subject to prescribed conditions; the subsection grants to that person for that year and says no more

§§ `s 14 Restriction on right to pay Class 3 contributions`

-- s 14(1): no person is entitled to pay a Class 3 contribution for a tax year if his earnings factor, or the aggregate of his earnings factors, for
-- that year (derived as the paragraphs say) equals or exceeds the qualifying earnings factor for that year.
-- src:566 | (1) No person shall be entitled to pay a Class 3 contribution in respect of any tax year if his earnings factor, or the aggregate of his earnings factors, for that year derived—
-- src:567 | (a) in the case of 1987-88 or any subsequent year, from earnings upon which Class 1 contributions have been paid or treated as paid or from Class 2 contributions actually paid; or
-- src:568 | (b) in the case of any earlier year, from contributions actually paid,
-- src:569 | is equal to or exceeds the qualifying earnings factor for that year; and regulations may provide for precluding the payment of Class 3 contributions in other cases.
@ref s 14(1) (src:566-569)
GIVEN `the person's earnings factor, or the aggregate of his earnings factors, for the tax year derived as mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b)` IS A NUMBER
      `the qualifying earnings factor for the tax year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 14(1) the person is entitled to pay a Class 3 contribution for the tax year` MEANS
    IF `the person's earnings factor, or the aggregate of his earnings factors, for the tax year derived as mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b)` AT LEAST `the qualifying earnings factor for the tax year`
    THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person shall be entitled to pay a Class 3 contribution in respect of any tax year if his earnings factor ... is equal to or exceeds the qualifying earnings factor for that year"
    ELSE NOTHING       -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a prohibition "if" the earnings factor reaches the qualifying level does not grant a right below it (below the level the prohibition does not apply, which is not a grant); "regulations may provide for precluding the payment of Class 3 contributions in other cases" points outside the text

-- s 13 with ss 1(6)(b) and 14(1): the whole answer on whether the person may pay a Class 3 contribution for the tax year.
-- src:525 | (1) The Treasury shall by regulations provide for earners and others, if over the age of 16, to be entitled if they so wish, but subject to any prescribed conditions, to pay Class 3 contributions; and, subject to the following provisions of this section, the amount of a Class 3 contribution shall be £18.40.
-- src:526 | (2) Payment of Class 3 contributions shall be allowed only with a view to enabling the contributor to satisfy ... conditions of entitlement to benefit by acquiring the requisite earnings factor for the purposes described in section 22 below.
@ref s 13(1) (src:525-526)
GIVEN bars IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
      grant IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 13 the Class 3 contribution may be paid once the bars are taken into account` MEANS
    IF any (GIVEN b YIELD b EQUALS JUST FALSE) bars THEN JUST FALSE ELSE grant    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): a bar's own no, passed on; ss 1(6)(b) and 14(1) carry the quoted words

-- s 14(3): repayable contributions under regulations under (2) are treated, for benefit entitlement, as not paid; no other repayable
-- contribution is implied to be treated as paid.
-- src:571 | (3) Contributions repayable by virtue of regulations under subsection (2) above shall, for the purpose of determining the contributor’s entitlement to any benefit, be treated as not having been paid (but nothing in this subsection shall be taken to imply that any other repayable contributions are to be treated for the purposes of benefit as having been paid).
@ref s 14(3) (src:571-571)
GIVEN `the contribution is repayable by virtue of regulations under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 14(3) the contribution is treated as not having been paid for the purpose of determining entitlement to any benefit` MEANS
    IF `the contribution is repayable by virtue of regulations under subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "nothing in this subsection shall be taken to imply that any other repayable contributions are to be treated for the purposes of benefit as having been paid"

-- s 14(4): where primary Class 1 contributions have been paid or treated as paid on any part of earnings, (1)(a) has effect as if they had been paid
-- on so much of the earnings as did not exceed the upper earnings limit.
-- src:572 | (4) Where primary Class 1 contributions have been paid or treated as paid on any part of a person’s earnings, subsection (1)(a) above shall have effect as if such contributions had been paid or treated as paid on so much of those earnings as did not exceed the upper earnings limit.
@ref s 14(4) (src:572-572)
GIVEN earnings IS A NUMBER
      `the upper earnings limit` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 14(4) the earnings on which primary Class 1 contributions are treated as paid for the purposes of subsection (1)(a)` MEANS min earnings `the upper earnings limit`

§§ `s 14A Class 3A contributions in return for units of additional pension`

-- s 14A(1A): the cut-off date is 5 April 2017 or, if later, the end of the 30-day period beginning with the day on which the person is sent information by
-- HMRC in response to a request made before 6 April 2017. The end of a 30-day period beginning with a day is that day plus 29 (fork F5: the day itself is day 1; the other reading counts from the next day).
-- src:577 | (1A) The cut-off date is—
-- src:578 | (a) 5th April 2017, or
-- src:579 | (b) if later the end of the 30-day period beginning with the day on which the person is sent information about Class 3A contributions by Her Majesty’s Revenue and Customs in response to a request made before 6th April 2017.
@ref s 14A(1A) (src:577-579)
GIVEN `the day on which the person is sent information about Class 3A contributions by Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs in response to a request made before 6 April 2017` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 14A(1A) the cut-off date` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day on which the person is sent information about Class 3A contributions by Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs in response to a request made before 6 April 2017`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN Date 5 4 2017
    WHEN JUST d THEN
        IF (d PLUS 29) GREATER THAN (Date 5 4 2017)
        THEN d PLUS 29
        ELSE Date 5 4 2017

-- s 14A(2): a person is eligible if (a) entitled to a Category A, B or D retirement pension or graduated retirement benefit, or (b) has deferred
-- entitlement to a Category A or B retirement pension or graduated retirement benefit. Whether a retirement pension is deferred is s 55(3) (ssc3: seam S10).
-- src:580 | (2) A person is eligible to pay a Class 3A contribution if the person—
-- src:581 | (a) is entitled to a Category A, Category B or Category D retirement pension or graduated retirement benefit, or
-- src:582 | (b) has deferred entitlement to a Category A or Category B retirement pension or graduated retirement benefit.
@ref s 14A(2) (src:580-582)
GIVEN `the person is entitled to a Category A, Category B or Category D retirement pension or graduated retirement benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 55(3) the retirement pension is deferred` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the graduated retirement benefit is deferred within the meaning of section 36(4A) of the National Insurance Act 1965` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 14A(2) the person is eligible to pay a Class 3A contribution` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is entitled to a Category A, Category B or Category D retirement pension or graduated retirement benefit` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 55(3) the retirement pension is deferred` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the graduated retirement benefit is deferred within the meaning of section 36(4A) of the National Insurance Act 1965` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 55(3) the retirement pension is deferred` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the pension is deferred is section 55(3)'s answer
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is eligible to pay a Class 3A contribution if the person (a) ... or (b) ..." (marginal reading M1(a))

-- s 14A(1): an eligible person is entitled to pay a Class 3A contribution before the cut-off date, in return for a unit of additional pension.
-- src:576 | (1) An eligible person is entitled to pay a Class 3A contribution before the cut-off date, in return for a unit of additional pension.
@ref s 14A(1) (src:576-576)
GIVEN `s 14A(2) the person is eligible to pay a Class 3A contribution` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the day of payment` IS A DATE
      `s 14A(1A) the cut-off date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 14A(1) the person is entitled to pay a Class 3A contribution on the day` MEANS
    IF `s 14A(2) the person is eligible to pay a Class 3A contribution` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the day of payment` LESS THAN `s 14A(1A) the cut-off date`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An eligible person is entitled to pay a Class 3A contribution before the cut-off date"; a person not eligible, or a payment on or after the cut-off date, is outside the grant

-- s 14A(5): a person (a) may pay Class 3A contributions on more than one occasion, but (b) may not obtain more than the maximum number of units of
-- additional pension (specified by the Treasury in regulations: an input).
-- src:585 | (5) A person—
-- src:586 | (a) may pay Class 3A contributions on more than one occasion, but
-- src:587 | (b) may not obtain more than the maximum number of units of additional pension.
-- src:588 | (6) The maximum number of units of additional pension that a person may obtain is to be specified by the Treasury in regulations.
@ref s 14A(5), s 14A(6) (src:585-588)
GIVEN `the person has already paid a Class 3A contribution on an earlier occasion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the units of additional pension the person has already obtained` IS A NUMBER
      `the units of additional pension the person would obtain by this payment` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum number of units of additional pension specified by the Treasury in regulations` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 14A(5) the person may pay a Class 3A contribution on this occasion` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the units of additional pension the person has already obtained` PLUS `the units of additional pension the person would obtain by this payment`) GREATER THAN `the maximum number of units of additional pension specified by the Treasury in regulations` THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): (b), "may not obtain more than the maximum number of units of additional pension"
        IF `the person has already paid a Class 3A contribution on an earlier occasion` THEN JUST TRUE    -- (a): "may pay Class 3A contributions on more than one occasion"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (5) speaks of paying "on more than one occasion"; the first payment is subsection (1)'s

-- src:589 | (7) In this section “deferred”, in relation to graduated retirement benefit, has the meaning given by section 36(4A) of the National Insurance Act 1965.
@ref s 14A(7) (src:589-589)
GIVEN `the benefit is deferred within the meaning given by section 36(4A) of the National Insurance Act 1965` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 14A(7) the graduated retirement benefit is deferred` MEANS
    IF `the benefit is deferred within the meaning given by section 36(4A) of the National Insurance Act 1965`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“deferred”, in relation to graduated retirement benefit, has the meaning given by section 36(4A) of the National Insurance Act 1965"

-- src:590 | (8) For the meaning of “deferred” in relation to a Category A or Category B retirement pension, see section 55(3) of this Act.
@ref s 14A(8) (src:590-590)
GIVEN `s 55(3) the retirement pension is deferred` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 14A(8) the Category A or Category B retirement pension is deferred` MEANS `s 55(3) the retirement pension is deferred`

§§ `s 14B Class 3A contributions: repayment`

-- src:594 | (3) A person is to be treated as never having had a unit of additional pension if the Class 3A contribution paid in respect of it is repaid.
@ref s 14B(3) (src:594-594)
GIVEN `the Class 3A contribution paid in respect of the unit is repaid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 14B(3) the person is treated as never having had the unit of additional pension` MEANS
    IF `the Class 3A contribution paid in respect of the unit is repaid`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is to be treated as never having had a unit of additional pension if the Class 3A contribution paid in respect of it is repaid" (marginal reading M1(a))
